WHAT THIS BRANCH ADDS

The `dgx-spark` branch (the default branch of this fork) carries, on top of
upstream v1.1.27 (merged, so this branch is a fast-forward of their main
plus these additions):

    Copyright (c) 2026 carlos patriawan
    Also under the MIT License.

    - the aarch64 port: NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10) and Grace on CUDA
      (src/kernels/cpu/portable.cpp, include/strata/platform/cpu_relax.hpp,
      the unified-memory expert pool and the ARM spin and store fence in
      src/core/, and the ARM handling in setup.py, maya.py and CMakeLists.txt)
    - the prompt path's allocation-failure recovery
      (include/strata/prefill/failure.hpp, src/prefill/, src/core/glm_prefill.cu,
      src/program/generate.cpp)
    - the token-size benchmark (tools/bench_tokens.py, BENCHMARK.md)
    - the Hugging Face publishing pipeline (docs/hf-dataset/,
      docs/hf-maya-s-v2-dgx-spark-README.md)

Everything else in this branch is upstream's, unchanged. The full account of
what the port changed, where each component comes from and what other people
contributed is in docs/DGX_SPARK_BUILD.md.

UPSTREAM'S RELEASES

Upstream v1.1.27 is merged into this branch (the merge commit says so), so
`dgx-spark` is upstream's `main` plus the additions above - a pull request
from it contains only this fork's work. Every upstream commit, release tag and
credit remains in the history untouched.

